    new='NEW proposed choice A: register this rider as an ordinary-extinguishable attached fire. Reuse the reviewed one self/helper extinguish Action or full immersion to end all present eligible ordinary-extinguishable attached fires on this creature, including suppressed records. No Sleight of Hand task or one-record restriction is added. Actual physical access, sufficient immersion and any explicit protected-fire exception retain their real requirements; a nonexistent water supply or mere declared splash is not full immersion. Other reviewed fire-periodic cures keep their actual scope and cost. The older one-record DEX-task treatment remains preserved as an unadopted alternative.'
    ck('Exact old Immolation treatment preserved and found once',imm.count(old)==1)
    imm=imm.replace(old,new)+'\n\nCURRENT FAMILY INTEGRATION: Register one stack group per original caster Immolation source with its one-active-rider cap. At each identical target END marker, all due ongoing-fire groups, including other registered source families, enter the accepted highest-expected-unmitigated-damage arbitration; source caps apply first, ties use earliest application then stable sequence. Only the winning eligible group damages; all due groups consume their scheduled tick, including losers and suppressed groups under their actual rules. Fire damage immunity does not remove an otherwise operative group from comparison. Each surviving eligible record with future ticks keeps its own due ending DEX save, including the accepted suppressed-record cure/save permission. Last consumed tick closes the finite record with no redundant save. Separate casters do not authorize several full fire packets at the same identical marker.'
